Aloy does not need to attack to trigger Discover. She is a Human Warrior rather than an artifact creature, so keep her safe behind your lines with reach and vigilance while your giant robotic beasts do the attacking. Discover X checks the greatest power among attacking artifact creatures at the moment attackers are declared, casting cards with mana value X or less for free or drawing them.
Bracket 3: the Game Changer cap is three, filled by Cyclonic Rift, Fierce Guardianship, and The One Ring. No mass land denial. Basalt Monolith, Forsaken Monument, and Walking Ballista provide a compact infinite finish that waits until turn 6 under house rules.

# The engine: Aloy and Discover
Aloy, Savior of Meridian :: whenever one or more artifact creatures attack, discover X, where X is greatest power among them. You can cast the discovered spell without paying its mana cost or put it into your hand.
Roaming Throne :: name Human or Warrior. Roaming Throne is an artifact creature that can attack, and it doubles Aloy's triggered ability so you discover twice every combat.
Genji Glove :: equips for {3} to grant double strike and an extra combat phase each turn. Attack with the equipped machine to discover once in the first combat, untap it, and attack again to discover a second time.
Cyberdrive Awakener :: turns all your noncreature mana rocks and utility artifacts into 4/4 flying artifact creatures for the turn, swinging over blockers and triggering Discover 4.
Simulacrum Synthesizer :: crafts Construct tokens whose power equals the number of artifacts you control whenever an artifact with mana value 3 or greater enters, generating 8/8 or 10/10 attackers that scale Discover into massive numbers.
Master of Etherium :: an artifact creature whose power equals the number of artifacts you control while buffing other artifact creatures by +1/+1.
Kappa Cannoneer :: ward {4} and unblockable when an artifact enters, growing each time to deliver huge unblockable Discover triggers.
Traxos, Scourge of Kroog :: a 7/7 trample artifact creature for four mana that untaps whenever you cast a historic spell, guaranteeing Discover 7 on every swing.
Ultron, Artificial Malevolence :: pay {2} whenever another nontoken artifact enters to create a copy of it, doubling up on beaters, mana rocks, or game-ending bombs.
Shuri, Wakandan Inventor :: discounts artifact spells by {1} and taps to make one artifact become a copy of your biggest artifact creature until end of turn.

# The giant machines
Blightsteel Colossus :: an 11/11 indestructible trampler with infect that discovers for 11 on attack and threatens to eliminate an opponent in a single swing.
Darksteel Colossus :: an 11/11 indestructible trampler that triggers Discover 11 and survives almost every damage-based or destroy sweeper.
Cityscape Leveler :: an 8/8 trampler that destroys a nonland permanent on cast and on attack while triggering Discover 8; unearth lets it return from the graveyard for a surprise swing.
Triplicate Titan :: a 9/9 flying, vigilance, trample Golem that discovers for 9 and leaves three 3/3 keyworded Golems behind if removed.
Krang, Utrom Warlord :: a 9/9 flying, trample, indestructible, haste threat that gives all your other artifact creatures flying, trample, indestructible, and haste.
Metalwork Colossus :: a 10/10 that costs {X} less where X is the noncreature artifact mana value on board, coming down for near-zero mana to trigger Discover 10.
Wurmcoil Engine :: a 6/6 deathtouch lifelink Wurm that stabilizes your life total, discovers for 6, and splits into two tokens on death.
Darksteel Forge :: makes all your artifacts indestructible, shielding your machines, lands, and mana rocks from sweeps and shatter effects.
Portal to Phyrexia :: forces each opponent to sacrifice three creatures on entry and reanimates a creature from any graveyard every upkeep; discovering into this completely crushes opposing boards.

# Infinite mana and the compact finish
Basalt Monolith + Forsaken Monument :: Forsaken Monument adds an extra {C} when Basalt taps for {C}{C}{C}, netting 4 mana; pay {3} to untap Basalt, netting infinite colorless mana
Basalt Monolith + Forsaken Monument + Walking Ballista :: infinite colorless mana into Walking Ballista shoots the entire table for lethal damage
Basalt Monolith + Forsaken Monument + Urza, Lord High Artificer :: infinite colorless mana into Urza activates his ability infinitely, exiling your library and casting every nonland card
Forsaken Monument :: doubles mana from colorless sources, gives colorless creatures +2/+2 to boost Discover triggers, and gains two life whenever you cast a colorless spell.
Basalt Monolith :: acts as early explosive ramp to accelerate Aloy or a big machine, and serves as half of the infinite mana engine.
Walking Ballista :: an artifact creature that removes problem creatures or planeswalkers early, can be tutored by Urza's Saga or Tezzeret, and acts as the game-ending outlet for infinite mana.
Urza, Lord High Artificer :: taps artifacts for blue mana, creates a Karn-struct token, and serves as an infinite mana sink to cast your entire library.
Under Bracket 3 rules, this infinite combo must wait until turn 6 or later. Spend turns 1 through 5 establishing ramp, casting Aloy, and discovering giant threats.

# Tutors and what to fetch
Fabricate -> Basalt Monolith :: when you need the combo engine or ramp
Fabricate -> Forsaken Monument :: when Basalt is already on board or you need to pump your colorless army
Fabricate -> Darksteel Forge :: when you need to make your entire artifact board untouchable
Fabricate -> Walking Ballista :: when you have infinite mana assembled and need the game-ender
Whir of Invention -> Portal to Phyrexia :: instant-speed wipe three creatures per opponent at end of turn
Whir of Invention -> The One Ring :: instant-speed protection and draw
Whir of Invention -> Basalt Monolith :: instant-speed combo piece directly onto the battlefield
Inventors' Fair -> Walking Ballista :: when you have infinite mana assembled and need the game-ender
Inventors' Fair -> Darksteel Forge :: when you need to protect your board from an incoming board wipe
Tezzeret, Cruel Captain -> Walking Ballista :: [-3] puts Ballista directly into your hand to close out the game
Tezzeret, Cruel Captain -> Sol Ring :: [-3] early when you need mana development
Urza's Saga -> Sol Ring :: early explosive acceleration on chapter III
Urza's Saga -> Walking Ballista :: direct fetch to the battlefield for the win on chapter III
Urza's Saga -> Sensei's Divining Top :: topdeck control to set up optimal Discover hits

# Utility engines and card flow
The One Ring :: grants protection from everything for a turn, stays on board as an artifact, and draws accelerating cards every turn cycle.
The Great Henge :: taps for two green, gains life, puts +1/+1 counters on entering creatures, and draws a card whenever a creature enters.
Chimil, the Inner Sun :: makes your spells uncounterable and discovers 5 at each of your end steps, providing relentless free card advantage.
Mystic Forge :: allows you to cast artifacts from the top of your library and exiles unwanted cards with {T} and 1 life.
Sensei's Divining Top :: smooths draws, manipulates the top of the library for Discover or Mystic Forge, and protects itself.
Unwinding Clock :: untaps all artifacts on each opponent's untap step, letting you use mana rocks, Top, and The One Ring repeatedly.
Padeem, Consul of Innovation :: gives all artifacts hexproof from opponents and draws an extra card on upkeep when you control the highest mana value artifact.
Emry, Lurker of the Loch :: mills cards on entry and taps to cast artifacts directly from your graveyard.
Master Transmuter :: returns an artifact to your hand to cheat any artifact (such as Blightsteel Colossus or Portal to Phyrexia) onto the battlefield for {U}.
Garruk's Uprising :: grants all your creatures trample and draws a card whenever a 4+ power creature enters.
Thought Monitor :: an affinity artifact creature that draws two cards and can attack in the air.
Thopter Spy Network :: generates a flying Thopter token every upkeep and draws cards when artifact creatures deal combat damage.
Iron Spider, Stark Upgrade :: puts +1/+1 counters on all artifact creatures and removes two counters to draw cards.

# Interaction and protection
Fierce Guardianship :: free noncreature counterspell while Aloy is in play to stop sweepers or targeted removal.
Cyclonic Rift :: the premier asymmetric board wipe; overload it on an opponent's end step to sweep away all blockers and swing for the win.
Desynchronization :: an instant-speed bounce spell that returns all non-historic permanents, leaving your artifacts and legendaries untouched.
Heroic Intervention :: gives all permanents hexproof and indestructible at instant speed against Shatterstorm or Farewell.
Mana Drain :: counters any spell and converts its mana cost into colorless mana on your next turn to fund a giant machine.
Counterspell :: clean two-mana interaction against critical threats.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: one-mana negation for noncreature spells.
Beast Within :: flexible instant removal hitting any permanent at the cost of a 3/3 Beast token.
Boseiju, Who Endures :: uncounterable channel land to destroy opposing artifacts, enchantments, or nonbasic lands.
Otawara, Soaring City :: uncounterable channel bounce hitting any opposing nonland permanent.
Sink into Stupor :: MDFC answering a spell or nonland permanent on the stack or battlefield, or played as an untapped blue land.
Bala Ged Recovery :: MDFC that recurs any card from the graveyard to hand, or played as a tapped green land.

# Opening hand and sequencing
A winning hand needs two to three lands, early ramp (Sol Ring, Mox Opal, Arcane Signet, Nature's Lore, or Three Visits), and either an early engine (Simulacrum Synthesizer, Kappa Cannoneer, Traxos) or card draw (Mystic Remora, The One Ring).
Turn 1-2: Deploy mana rocks or land ramp to reach four to five mana quickly. Drop a cost reducer like Etherium Sculptor or Shuri if in hand.
Turn 3-4: Cast Aloy or a large artifact creature. If Aloy is already out, deploying Traxos, Kappa Cannoneer, or an affinity beater lets you declare attackers on the following turn and start Discovering immediately.
Turn 5+: Swing with your artifact machines. Discover chains into additional free threats, mana rocks, or card advantage. Hold up Fierce Guardianship, Heroic Intervention, or Cyclonic Rift to protect your board.
Turn 6+: If combat is locked down or you need to close immediately, tutor and assemble Basalt Monolith + Forsaken Monument for infinite mana into Walking Ballista or Urza.
